      "title": "Begin with the family, then the policy",
      "narration": "Marcus and Elena sit down with their household budget. They want the children to stay in their home and finish school if either parent dies. The first step is fact gathering: income, expenses, debts, dependents, existing coverage, savings, goals and an affordable premium. Include unpaid work such as childcare and household management. Losing that support can create a replacement cost even without losing a paycheck. The agent should understand who depends on each person and for how long. A product name or an income multiplier cannot answer those questions by itself.",
