      "title": "Cash accumulation and estate liquidity are different uses",
      "text": "Cash accumulation concerns accessible policy values during life, subject to product terms. Estate liquidity concerns having funds when obligations arise after death. Estate conservation concerns preserving assets rather than selling them under pressure. A personally owned mortgage-protection life policy can provide a beneficiary funds to address a mortgage, while credit life has a debt-linked structure taught separately.",
